cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "matisse"
abstract: >-
  A C++23 library that reads the definition of a real tokenizer, decides where its output can be cut with certainty, and
  encodes text in parallel by cutting only there, with token ids byte-identical to the sequential encoding. The first
  version covers GPT-2, cl100k_base, o200k_base and Llama 3, whose pre-tokenizer patterns have exact verifiers, and
  encodes a text that arrives in parts as a stream, returning each id once no continuation of the text can change it.
keywords:
  - tokenization
  - byte-pair encoding
  - pre-tokenization
  - parallel encoding
  - C++
